KONOHAGAKURE — LAND OF FIRE CIVILIAN PROTECTION POLICY

The foremost duty of a shinobi of the Leaf is the protection of the village and the civilians of the Land of Fire.

Provisions:
- Shinobi will not endanger non-combatants in the pursuit of a mission objective unless the greater safety of the village demands it, and then only under authorization.
- Civilian settlements within the Land of Fire may request protection through the Daimyo's court or directly at the village gate for urgent threats.
- The Will of Fire obligates every shinobi to shield the next generation — civilian children included.
- Bandit suppression and disaster relief within the borders are standing D- to C-rank tasking.

Harm to Fire Country civilians through negligence is a disciplinary matter reviewed by the Village Council.
Issued by the Office of the Hokage.
